{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. It requires comparing all pairwise differences between the outcomes of Lottery A and Lottery B. The outcomes of Lottery A are: 6000€ (25%), 0€ (75%). The outcomes of Lottery B are: 4000€ (25%), 2000€ (25%), and 0€ (50%). To compute the sum of all pairwise differences, we consider each outcome in A versus each outcome in B: (6000-4000)=2000, (6000-2000)=4000, (6000-0)=6000, (0-4000)=-4000, (0-2000)=-2000, (0-0)=0. The sum of these differences is 2000+4000+6000-4000-2000+0 = 6000. A positive sum would favor A, a negative sum would favor B. Here, the sum is positive, so the reason would prefer Lottery A. The relevant information (the outcomes) is available, so the reason can be applied.",
